  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "PLD-01",
      "claim": "Ke in the existing FSC-0105 local branch imports j$t; the initial Program exports z0r as j$t.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "local-import",
        "local-call",
        "initial-esm-export-j$t",
        "initial-esm-definition-j$t"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PLD-02",
      "claim": "z0r calls tI with projectType local, then emits electron-add-new-workspace-root-option with an empty payload. It has no return/await/catch for registration. tI returns or updates an in-scope flow record and emits a lifecycle step when newly allocated; this is not a project creation result.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "initial-esm-definition-j$t",
        "lifecycle-flow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PLD-03",
      "claim": "The matching MMe handler awaits projectFolderPicker.createOrSelectProject(e,t.root). Its constructor creates the Program-bound Mje with host, windowManager and projectsManager. This closes the saved handler receiver definition at the source level, conditional on message delivery to this handler.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "add-root-handler-case",
        "picker-construction",
        "message-owner-constructor",
        "picker-definition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PLD-04",
      "claim": "The local picker chooses/validates a root and calls createOrSelectLocalProjects([root]); cancellation/no result emits workspace-root-option-add-canceled. Success emits workspace-root-option-added with new/existing identity fields, then navigate-to-route /. Awaited errors have no local catch/finally in this method; this does not prove upstream error behavior.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "picker-definition",
        "picker-add-method",
        "create-or-select-method"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PLD-05",
      "claim": "The reviewed picker registration path is distinct from projects.createLocal. The qHe createOrSelectLocalProjects implementation requests roots, selects the first returned project and publishes local-project/order/selection updates. createLocal separately parses appearance/name/sources/initGit/setActive, can allocate a default root and returns projectId/rootPaths. Actual injected manager identity, backend success and durable effects remain unobserved.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "picker-add-method",
        "create-or-select-method",
        "create-local-comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PLD-06",
      "claim": "The sibling k$t export is B0r, which dispatches open-create-remote-project-modal. It is a separate remote entry; neither it nor WSL creation establishes local createLocal equivalence.",
      "sourceIds": [
        "initial-esm-export-k$t",
        "initial-esm-definition-k$t"
      ]
    }
  ],
